      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The physiology and pathology of dysmenorrhea in adolescent girls has become clear in the past 5 years. Although the prime cause of the disorder has not been identified, the obvious rise in PGF2 alpha prostaglandins is an objective biologic sign. As a result, more specific treatment has become possible with more definite and established care of this \"condition\" which is often distressing to the teenage girl affected."},
